    "created_at": "2016-11-07T19:49:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-07T19:49:25Z",
    "body": "It would be really great if the standards venue didn't affect the shape of the resulting API. Sounds like the three things raised in this thread have a path towards resolution. Would it be reasonable to start a policy of doing things in a more ES-type style when new APIs come up (sounds like enumerability is the big one here)? For enumerability on the JS side, there seems to be a strong feeling in TC39 that we couldn't add more enumerable methods to existing objects without breaking existing code.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
